    "sections": [
      {
        "type": "text",
        "content": "Q: The Winged Serpent stands as one of the most bizarre genre mashups of 1980s B-movies - combining film noir, monster horror, and Aztec mythology in grimy New York City locations. Director Larry Cohen, known for socially conscious exploitation films like <a href=\"/movie/28153\" class=\"movie-title\" data-tmdb-id=\"28153\">It's Alive</a> (1974), crafts a uniquely gritty take on the kaiju formula. The film's greatest asset is Michael Moriarty's unhinged performance as Jimmy Quinn, a small-time crook who discovers the nest of an ancient Aztec dragon-god in the Chrysler Building. His manic, improvised scenes create an unsettling counterpoint to David Carradine's stoic police detective."
      },
